 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 526533,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which represents a reasonable value for the area of the top of a kitchen table: 1,800 mm<sup>2</sup>, 1,800 cm<sup>2</sup>, or <span data-math=\"\\text{1,800 m}^2\">\\text{1,800 m}^2</span>?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A meter is roughly the length of a yardstick. An area of 1,800 square meters would be larger than many homes. Now decide between the other measurements.</p>\n<p>Suppose it was a square table. Find the measure of one side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {1,800{\\rm{\\ mm}^2}} \\approx 42.4{\\rm{\\ mm}} = 4.24\\ {\\rm cm}\"></span></p>\n<p>This would be less than the width of your hand.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {1,800{\\rm{\\ cm}^2}} \\approx 42.4{\\rm{\\ cm}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The 42.4 cm table would work.</p>\n<p>The 1,800 square centimeter table is the best choice.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "1,800 cm<sup>2</sup>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
